r.type/math "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "65c7445f65130fe4c828044f5045b651566096bf51c03481ccccb54865a65ef6" "basis" 1470 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "65c7445f65130fe4c828044f5045b651566096bf51c03481ccccb54865a65ef6" "basis" 1470 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "65c7445f65130fe4c828044f5045b651566096bf51c03481ccccb54865a65ef6" "basis" 1470 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "65c7445f65130fe4c828044f5045b651566096bf51c03481ccccb54865a65ef6" "basis" 1470 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|=3\\cdot 5=15.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040832/state.json" "file_sha256" "65c7445f65130fe4c828044f5045b651566096bf51c03481ccccb54865a65ef6" "basis" 1470 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linea