1"} {"question" "q-69952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The $4$th row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 11 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{41}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+0\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-69952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8e69abdd07ca8eda110c9aa413b623ca26ba5c516ac870e6814d079e7528257"} {"question" "q-69952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-69952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-69952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3+2 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|=3\\cdot 5=15.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8e69abdd07ca8eda110c9aa413b623ca26ba5c516ac870e6814d079e7528257"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "17"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-70108" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{21}+5\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-3-0)+5(-6-4) \\\\  & =3-50 \\\\  & =-47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+5\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-2)-5(-8-4) \\\\  & =-2+60 \\\\  & =58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-47+58=11.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8e69abdd07ca8eda110c9aa413b623ca26ba5c516ac870e6814d079e7528257"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-52"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+0\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+3\\cdot {C}_{24} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7-0 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=3(-7)=-21.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8e69abdd07ca8eda110c9aa413b623ca26ba5c516ac870e6814d079e7528257"} {"question" "q-77800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-21"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "36"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-77800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-21"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-42095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate\n$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"question" "q-42095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The $3$rd row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+1\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{3+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{31}+2\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1-2)-2(2-4) \\\\  & =-1+4 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+(-4)\\cdot {C}_{22}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4(2+3)+2(1+6) \\\\  & =-20+14 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 3-(-6)=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/state.json" "file_sha256" "28510feacc81d77c214a31a7af6b8f46abb77cd97a0c7ce2c9b714fa6198ffb1"} {"quest